    LLM: 'Game: 4-Card Brag. Type: Vying. Rules: 4 dealt, 3 kept. Hierarchy: Prial > Running Flush > Run. Half-price blind betting. Choice phase added to parent 3-card game.',
    Player: 'You were dealt the 3♠, 3♣, King of Hearts, and 3♦. You have a Prial of 3s—the highest hand in the game! Discard the King and prepare to build a massive pot.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by forming the best three-card hand from the four dealt, or by forcing others to fold.',
    gameplay: "1. **Selection**: Players receive 4 cards and discard 1. 2. **Vying**: Standard Brag betting follows. Players choose to play 'Blind' (without looking at their chosen 3) or 'See'. 3. **Ranks**: Prial > Running Flush > Run > Flush > Pair > High Card.",
    keyRules: [
      'The choice of which three cards to keep is the only skill difference from 3-Card Brag.',
      'Blind players bet half-price.',
      'Equal hands favor the player who remained Blind longer.',
